.TH "OBSIDIAN-ANKI-FLASHCARDS" "1" "2026-11-06" "Homelab ops"
.SH NAME
obsidian-anki-flashcards \- Process changed Obsidian notes through the existing review and Anki workflow.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obsidian-anki-flashcards
[arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Process changed Obsidian notes through the existing review and Anki workflow.
Established names and consumer paths are preserved. No hardware or service action was executed for documentation verification.
.SH INTERFACE
.SS /Users/iragonforce/.local/bin/obsidian-anki-flashcards
Source: hosts/qubit/files/.local/bin/obsidian-anki-flashcards
.nf
group.add_argument("--baseline", action="store_true", help="Register existing notes without generating anything")
group.add_argument("--once", action="store_true", help="Process changed notes once")
group.add_argument("--patch-reviewer", action="store_true", help="Allow full rewrites with protection warnings")
group.add_argument("--install-agent", action="store_true", help="Write the macOS LaunchAgent")
parser.add_argument("--vault", type=Path, default=DEFAULT_VAULT)
parser.add_argument("--reviewer", type=Path, default=DEFAULT_REVIEWER)
parser.add_argument("--state-dir", type=Path, default=DEFAULT_STATE)
parser.add_argument("--limit", type=int, default=1)
parser.add_argument("--now", action="store_true", help="Bypass edit quiet period for a deliberate manual test")
parser.add_argument("--note", help="Process one vault-relative path when it differs from baseline")
parser.add_argument("--auto-apply", action="store_true", help="Apply full rewrites in iCloud with approval and backups")
parser.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=420)
.fi

.SH DEPENDENCIES
Use the interpreter in the source shebang and the existing host packages and services referenced in that source. Host configuration and private credentials remain on their original host.
.SH OPERATIONS
Before changing behavior, inspect inventory/audit-2026-11-06/qubit.json for recorded consumers and the source above for exact dependency paths. Never invoke a power, desktop, network, credential, notification, or storage operation merely to test it.
